econd I'm gonna  explain why Point number one is that  Zeke basically thought of him here in  the same way King Fritz did in that he  thought of her as a slave lacking free  will that he could use for his own  purposes even until the end he never  acknowledged her as a real human being  whereas from the start Aaron saw her as  a person and couldn't believe that she'd  been here alone this whole time he  understood that it must have been Agony  to be in this realm of being orders for  thousands of years and unlike Zeke he  tried to offer her a choice rather than  simply viewing her as a tool  Point number two is that yamir was  clearly waiting for someone to free her  from this pain because after serving  other people our whole life I guess she  had to be reminded that it was okay to  exercise her own free will from her  point of view lashing out of the world  is clearly more appealing than spending  another 100 years trapped in the past  Dimension which is what would inevitably  happen if she follows these  euthanization plan  now before we move on to the amazing  reveal of Aaron's founding Titan there  were a few bits of trivia that I thought  were worth mentioning to begin the name  of this episode is from you 2000 years  ago which is a reference to the first  episode of Attack on Titan which was  called To You 2000 years from now the  names of these titles make it sound like  you may have sent something to Aaron in  the first episode which he then received  in this episode and one interpretation  is that it's referring to the memories  of her life story which he likely  received when they made contact  alternatively it could be referring to  the power she gave him to start the  rumbling or it might simply be referring  to the fact that she's been waiting for  2 000 years for someone like him to  arrive  next up earlier in the episode 3D  mentioned a story that she should be a  lady-like person like the girl in the  book and this is what directly led to  her overly kind personality that we saw  in the first couple Seasons the girl in  the book was called Cresta which is the  same fake name that Historia used when  she joined the cadets and it wasn't  until she met a Titan shifter called  yumea that she gained the courage to act  as her true self  finally the last thing to point out is  that the concepts in this episode are  heavily derived from Norse mythology  whether it be the world tree Ragnarok  the nine Titans corresponding with the  nine Realms or the fact that yamir is  the name of the first Giant in both  universes the connection likely runs  even deeper than just this however my  understanding of Norse pathology is  limited to my unfinished playthrough of  God of War and the MCU for that reason I  really can't go into any more detail but  I'm sure there is someone out there who  knows all about this stuff  anyhow moving on to the rest of the  episode in the real world only a second  did pass since Gabby blew off Aaron's  head in this moment here the source of  all living matter jumps out of his spine  to connect with his brain granting him  the true power of the founding Titan  thanks to you Mia's blessing almost  immediately following this the first  thing he does is crumble all the  hardening on parodies collapsing the  walls that have been there for over a  century as some of the hardening falls  down in Gabby's Direction Aaron begins  his weird transformation which was  unusual for a few reasons not only is  his new Titan significantly larger and  more bony than any type in history but  it also takes on a similar shape to the  hallucinogenia its bizarre appearance is  the result of Aaron transforming while  in this condition because the source of  all living matter had no choice but to  improvise and make a new body based on  its own image if Aaron had made contact  with Zeke when his body was whole then I  can guarantee you this sent to be Titan  never would have happened but because of  what Gabby did this is 